  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "Large volunteer army (~560,000) with a two-front posture: conventional deterrence against India along the LoC and border, and long-running counter-terrorism in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Balochistan against the TTP, ISIS-K and Baloch separatists. Equipment mixes Chinese (VT-4, SH-15, Z-10ME), US (M113, MaxxPro, AH-1F, M109) and Ukrainian (T-80UD) sources. Fought India in May 2025 (missiles, drones, artillery) and clashed with the Afghan Taliban on the border in October 2025.",
    "squad_size": 10,
    "fireteam": "Infantry section of ~10 with MG3 group; Frontier Corps and SSG operate smaller teams. Game: 8 in four pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Intelligence-based counter-terror raids in mountain villages (early-game contracts)",
      "Convoy and picket defence against ambushes and IEDs (map hazard) in the tribal districts",
      "Artillery duels and drone use along the LoC",
      "Armoured counter-strikes in the Punjab plains",
      "SSG special forces hostage rescue and raids"
    ],
